  - dialogueID: '"toybox_interact"'
    lines:
    - text: Dad was... particular about me cleaning up my playroom. He engineered
        one of his crazy machines so that the basement door wouldn't open unless
        all my toys were put away. I remember one time I threw one of the toys under
        the door, the pressure plate system went off and closed the door, and I wasn't
        able it open it again without that last toy. Dad didn't let me down there
        for a week while he was fixing it, and I never did get that toy back.
      speakerName: 
